<title>AUSTRIA: Buba's Sievert says German M3 could hit target.</title>
<headline>Buba's Sievert says German M3 could hit target.</headline>
<dateline>SALZBURG, Austria 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Olaf Sievert said on Friday he could not rule out the possibility that German M3 money supply growth, the central bank's key policy guide, would hit its four to seven percent target corridor this year.</p>
<p>&quot;It's not sure yet how the money supply indicator will develop. It cannot be ruled out that M3 will be on target,&quot; he told a bankers' conference.</p>
</text>
